[
{
  type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenClaw is a multi-channel AI gateway.

To get started:

1. Onboarding:
   Log in as the account that will run the OpenClaw service. Use this same
   account for every command marked with "$" below so configuration and
   pairing data are stored in the service account's home directory.
   Run the interactive onboarding wizard to set up your workspace:
   $ openclaw onboard

2. Telegram Integration:
   * Message @BotFather on Telegram and use /newbot.
   * Note the API Token and set it:
     $ openclaw config set channels.telegram.botToken "YOUR_TOKEN"

3. FreeBSD Service:
   As root, set the service account before enabling and starting the service.
   Replace USERNAME with the account used for onboarding above. The service
   defaults to root if openclaw_user is not configured.
   # sysrc openclaw_user="USERNAME"
   # sysrc openclaw_enable="YES"
   # service openclaw start

4. Account Pairing:
   * Open your new bot on Telegram and click "Start".
   * Approve the pairing request on the host:
     $ openclaw pairing approve telegram <CODE>

5. Web UI (Dashboard):
   Access the management dashboard:
   $ openclaw dashboard
   By default, it is available at http://localhost:18789

For more information, see https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw

Slow model requests can use models.providers.<id>.timeoutSeconds in the
existing provider configuration. This covers HTTP and stream timeouts;
any shorter agent or run timeout still applies. Use explicit provider
model entries when configuring this setting.

The optional memory-lancedb plugin requires native libraries that are not
available on FreeBSD. This package does not bundle that external plugin.

EOM
},
{
  type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "2026.9.4"
  message: <<EOM
The EXTEND_AI_TIMEOUT and EXTEND_TYPING_TTL_TIMEOUT port options have been
removed. Their compiled-JavaScript replacements no longer match upstream.
For a slow model server, configure models.providers.<id>.timeoutSeconds
in its existing provider entry. The upstream typing keepalive now refreshes
its safety deadline while a reply is active.

Use the same account for configuration commands and the rc.d service.
EOM
